  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle DEF\\), \\(\\angle A=\\angle D\\), \\(\\angle B=\\angle E\\), and \\(BC=EF\\). Which congruence criterion can be used?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "ASA",
    "B": "AAS",
    "C": "SAS",
    "D": "SSS"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(BC\\) is opposite \\(\\angle A\\), and \\(EF\\) is opposite \\(\\angle D\\). Two angles and the side opposite one of them are respectively equal, so AAS applies.",
